 "result_text": "I fixed the crash in `parse_get_bucket_location` in `botocore/handlers.py`. I haven't run it or any tests.\n\nWhen the response is an error, the handler no longer tries to read the HTTP body. A stubbed client error has no body, which is why `http_response.content` failed with `'NoneType' object has no attribute 'stream'`. The new check returns early whenever the parsed response contains an `Error` key. That should let `add_client_error('get_bucket_location', 'NoSuchBucket')` raise the normal `ClientError`, like `get_bucket_logging` already does.\n\nA real error response from S3 also contains an `Error` key, so it now skips the XML parsing too. That seems right, since there's no `LocationConstraint` to extract from an error.\n\nI didn't add a test, as you asked.",
